course: dictionary
lesson: 10704
title: Unsuccessful and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unsuccessful is built from parts you may know. The start, un-, means not. Success means getting what you wanted. So unsuccessful means not getting what you wanted, or failing. Look at «an unsuccessful attempt»: the clue is that the attempt did not work.
explain: Context helps you check. In «unsuccessful experiment», the scientist tried something and it did not give the result planned. In maths, «7 of the 10 tries were unsuccessful» tells you the number of failures, so the other 3 tries must have worked.
explain: In a formal letter, unsuccessful is a polite word for rejected. «We regret that your application was unsuccessful» means the school or company has said no. Swap your meaning into the sentence: «We regret that your application was rejected» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Unsuccessful means not achieving what was wanted or planned; failing.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unsuccessful is the opposite of successful.
fact: In a letter about a job or a place, unsuccessful means rejected.
fact: In school, an attempt or experiment can be unsuccessful and still teach you something.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The first attempt was unsuccessful, so we tried again.» What does unsuccessful mean here? | Hidden under the table | It was the best attempt of all | Very fast and clever | *It did not get the result we wanted
exercise: Maths: «7 of the 10 tries were unsuccessful.» How many of the 10 tries were successful? | 17 | 10 | 7 | *3
exercise: A letter says «we regret that your application was unsuccessful». What does this mean? | You got the job or place | *Your application was rejected | Your application was sent early | The letter is for a different child
test: Which word is the opposite of successful? | Lucky | Clever | *Unsuccessful | Careful
test: The prefix un- means not. What does «unsuccessful» mean as a whole? | Very successful | Hopeful | *Not achieving what was wanted | Not kept
exam: «His experiment was unsuccessful, so he wrote down what went wrong.» What does the sentence show? | The experiment was a huge success | He forgot to write anything down | The experiment was finished early | *The experiment did not work as planned
